        "text": "The singular value decomposition combines the polar decomposition and the spectral theorem.\n\nCorollary 2.4: (Singular value decomposition) Let $A$ be a square matrix.\nThen there exist unitary matrices $U$ and $V$, and a diagonal matrix $D$ with non-negative entries such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{equation*}\nA=U D V \\tag{2.80}\n\\end{equation*}\n$$\n\nThe diagonal elements of $D$ are called the singular values of $A$."
